From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:30:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): let the running post-merge gate finish

Keep one pending run and preserve the existing ref groups.
Pin the concurrency policy with an xtask integration test.

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>

Fixes #1922
---
 .github/workflows/post-merge.yml              |  6 ++---
 docs/decisions/1922-post-merge-concurrency.md | 17 ++++++++++++++
 xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs         | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 docs/decisions/1922-post-merge-concurrency.md
 create mode 100644 xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs

diff --git a/.github/workflows/post-merge.yml b/.github/workflows/post-merge.yml
index 182910ba5..d714f97d9 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/post-merge.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/post-merge.yml
@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@
 # pull_request, pull_request_target or schedule (maintainer, 2026-11-13: "Can
 # we setup a build test post merge using local gh runner?"; a push to main
 # only carries merged, reviewed code, so no fork can run code on the runner).
-# Sharing the one runner with the cut: this workflow yields. A burst of merges
-# tests only the newest head (cancel-in-progress), and a run skips itself
+# Sharing the one runner with the cut: this workflow yields. The running gate
+# finishes; newer merges replace the single pending run. A run skips itself
 # (green, with a notice) while a cut.yml run is queued or running or a
 # release/vX.Y.Z PR from this repo is open (.github/scripts/post-merge-skip.sh).
 # The release gate of the cut covers main's state then. A cut therefore never
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ permissions:
 # cancelled by) the gate of main.
 concurrency:
   group: post-merge-${{ github.event_name == 'push' && 'main' || inputs.ref || 'main' }}
-  cancel-in-progress: true
+  cancel-in-progress: false
 
 jobs:
   gate:
diff --git a/docs/decisions/1922-post-merge-concurrency.md b/docs/decisions/1922-post-merge-concurrency.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..5b52aaf80
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/1922-post-merge-concurrency.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## #1922 - Keep the running post-merge gate
+
+**Decided:** Set `cancel-in-progress: false`. Keep the existing concurrency
+group, which separates main from other refs.
+
+**Why:** A later merge must let the running gate finish and report its result.
+GitHub keeps one pending run per group. A newer run replaces that pending run,
+so a merge batch cannot create an unlimited queue.
+
+**Dropped:** A separate group for each commit would create a long queue.
+Automatic bisect after a failed gate is outside this issue's scope.
+
+**Cost to change later:** Change one setting. This choice uses more runner time
+and can delay the result for the latest commit by one gate run.
+
+**Not exercised:** The local test checks the workflow setting. An actual merge
+batch must confirm the Actions queue behaviour after this change merges.
diff --git a/xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs b/xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..bf2448b5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+// Provenance: issue #1922 and the repository's post-merge workflow contract.
+use std::{fs, path::Path};
+
+#[test]
+fn post_merge_preserves_running_gate() {
+    let path = Path::new(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")).join("../.github/workflows/post-merge.yml");
+    let workflow = fs::read_to_string(path).expect("read the post-merge workflow");
+    let concurrency = workflow
+        .split_once("\nconcurrency:\n")
+        .expect("the workflow has top-level concurrency")
+        .1
+        .split("\njobs:\n")
+        .next()
+        .expect("read the concurrency block");
+    assert!(concurrency.lines().any(|line| line == "  group: post-merge-${{ github.event_name == 'push' && 'main' || inputs.ref || 'main' }}"),
+        "keep main pushes together and other refs in their own groups");
+    assert!(
+        concurrency
+            .lines()
+            .any(|line| line == "  cancel-in-progress: false"),
+        "a later merge must not cancel the running post-merge gate"
+    );
+}
